      "name": "D11",
      "label": "GPIO11 (Button)",
      "codeName": "D11",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_input",
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "button"
      ],
      "notes": "BOOT button — onboard bootloader-select pushbutton, also usable as a general input when application code is running. Already aliased as D11 in this board's pins_arduino.h (so it already carries full digital_input/digital_output/pwm_output capability via the normal alias path) — this entry adds the button tag. Not broken out to a physical header pad (internally dedicated to the onboard pushbutton). Confirmed via CircuitPython's pins.c for this board (MP_QSTR_BUTTON -> pin_GPIO11, MP_QSTR_D11 -> pin_GPIO11) and Adafruit's own pinouts/digital-input guides (\"This button... also functions as a GPIO input via board.BUTTON in code\"; read via digitalio.DigitalInOut with an internal pull-up)."
    },
